  "scriptId": "pl-08-two-articles-equal-gain-loss",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Two Articles, Equal Gain and Loss, and Overall Result",
    "description": "Understand why equal gain and loss percentages on two equal selling prices do not cancel, and solve paired-item transactions.",
    "teachingApproach": "Contrast three superficially similar paired-item structures: equal selling prices with ±x%, equal rupee gain/loss, and a shared total-cost split. Derive the x²/100 shortcut from reconstructed costs so it is used only where valid.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach paired transactions with a total-cost view. Cover two articles sold at the same S.P., one at x% gain and one at x% loss, derive the inevitable loss and connect it to the book’s x²/100 rule. Also cover unequal gain/loss percentages, equal absolute profit and loss at two selling prices, recovering C.P. as the midpoint when gain and loss amounts are equal, and splitting a total cost between two items from the overall result. Learners should not average percentages blindly; they must reconstruct the cost bases."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn two articles, equal gain and loss, and overall result.\n\nTwo articles are sold for the same price. One gives 20% profit and the other 20% loss. It feels as if they should cancel — but they do not.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Equal profit and loss percentages do not always cancel. The classic trap appears when two items are sold for the same price.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two items sell for ₹120 each.\nFirst at 20% profit → C.P. = 120/1.20 = ₹100.\nSecond at 20% loss → C.P. = 120/0.80 = ₹150.\nTotal C.P. ₹250, S.P. ₹240 → 4% loss.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
